email queries to me, I can handle, just as quickly as I am handling this 
response to you.  snail mail is a lot harder, since I have trouble getting 
around to the whole process of pen-to-paper (or 
computer-keyboard-to-envelope, if you prefer).  It is the snail mail 
queries we aren't handling.  Net-based queries - our ISP was even able to 
handle the massive number of queries from being slash-dotted, or whatever 
it was called, a couple years ago.  But while massive amounts were 
downloaded, and Lojban List grew somewhat, that did not turn into more 
personal queries, nor into more sales.  We've had more book orders in the 
last month than in any month since shortly after the book was published.

The problem with any sort of advertising that generates orders, especially 
if they are not orders for the one product (the book) that we are able to 
relatively easily prepare and ship from stock in hand, is in my time to 
fill the orders.

